    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_10",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Kiddieland Amusement Park was an amusement park located just west of Chicago at the corner of North Avenue and First Avenue in Melrose Park, Illinois. It was home to several classic rides including the \"Little Dipper\" roller coaster, which opened in 1950. The park closed on September 27, 2009, and was demolished in 2010 to make way for a new Costco store.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.9999999961470136,
      "temperature": 0.9999999961470136,
